# Ignore list for `docker build -f apps/api/Dockerfile .`, whose context is the
# WORKSPACE ROOT (the only image built from this repository). A root
# `.dockerignore` is read by every builder — BuildKit, the legacy builder,
# kaniko, buildah — so secrets stay out of the context whichever one runs.
# Paths are relative to the workspace root.

# Only the API image is built from this context.
apps/desktop

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage

# TypeScript incremental build cache. `dist` above does not cover it — tsc puts
# it at the project root once `rootDir` is pinned. Copying a developer's or a
# deploy host's stale cache into the build context makes the in-image
# `pnpm build` emit nothing while still exiting 0, producing an image with no
# application code. `git reset --hard` on a deploy host does not remove
# untracked files, so one left behind there would poison every later build.
# `**/` because Docker ignore patterns are path-segment-scoped and a bare `*`
# would not match a nested cache.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
**/.gitignore
**/.env
**/.env.*
!apps/api/.env.example
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/*.log
.github
.claude
apps/api/.claude
apps/api/.github
apps/api/.zap
apps/api/test
apps/api/docs
**/README.md
**/AGENTS.md
**/CLAUDE.md
apps/api/docker-compose.yml
apps/api/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.prettierrc
apps/api/eslint.config.mjs
# Private keys and certificates never belong in the image.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
